# taihen-0001: build the pinned taiHEN (309b3800bcb8) against the current
# VitaSDK (GCC 15.2, 2026-08 headers). Upstream drift this fixes: process
# context became a 12-byte struct (int[3] no longer matches); the memcpy
# helpers moved to explicit ksceKernelCopy{To,From}UserProc with pointer
# arguments; ksceKernelCpuUnrestrictedMemcpy and the Cpu cache/interrupt
# wrappers were replaced (SuspendIntr/ResumeIntr, DcacheCleanInvalidateRange,
# IcacheInvalidateRange); the sbl headers moved to kernel/{acmgr,aimgr}.h
# (acmgr.h keeps a ksceSblACMgrIsShell back-compat macro); hen.c needs
# kernel/sysroot.h for the GetProcessTitleId macro; substitute's execmem.c
# (inside the substitute gitlink, patched here across the submodule) used the
# removed unrestricted memcpy and the old Rx-macro argument order.
# The module is built only so vita-elf-export can derive libtaihen_stub.a
# from exports.yml; the device runs the community taiHEN module, so these
# branches only have to compile and link. uintptr_t->pointer int-conversion
# warnings in the user wrappers are downgraded in the script, not here.
